WEBVTT

00:12.512 --> 00:14.514
I'm gonna go get a drink.

00:14.597 --> 00:16.850
Amamiya. I'm coming too.

00:24.524 --> 00:25.984
Without exchanging a word...

00:26.526 --> 00:28.027
We've arrived.

00:38.830 --> 00:45.336
Hey, do you think they'll be surprised
if they come back to find nobody here?

00:45.420 --> 00:46.880
Shall we?

00:46.963 --> 00:48.339
THESE TWO HAVE
COMPLETELY GONE OFF TRACK

00:50.550 --> 00:51.885
- So cold...
- So hot...

00:51.968 --> 00:52.969
THUMP THUMP

00:53.052 --> 00:54.095
Minato!

00:55.930 --> 00:57.223
Kenta. Hello.

00:57.724 --> 00:59.726
You doing those questions I gave you?

01:01.186 --> 01:02.395
Seniors.

01:03.063 --> 01:05.732
- Scurry, scurry.
- I was doing them till just a second ago.

01:05.815 --> 01:07.108
You sure about that?

01:08.860 --> 01:10.028
Is this one of your juniors?

01:10.111 --> 01:11.571
Yep. Cutie, isn't he?

01:11.654 --> 01:13.823
Does Kenta look out for you
like he should?

01:13.907 --> 01:16.868
He loves to pretend he's all that,
but he couldn't be farther from "that."

01:16.951 --> 01:18.411
I beg your pardon?

01:18.495 --> 01:20.246
FADE

01:20.330 --> 01:21.790
- See ya.
- Bye-bye.

01:21.873 --> 01:22.874
See you.

01:23.708 --> 01:24.709
POKE OUT

01:24.793 --> 01:26.628
- Are you done?
- Hikawa?

01:27.462 --> 01:30.089
You could have
just been yourself, you know.

01:30.590 --> 01:31.841
It's not that.

01:32.425 --> 01:33.927
It's not that I wasn't being myself,

01:34.010 --> 01:35.929
it's just that I don't know
those older people.

01:36.930 --> 01:38.181
Were you scared?

01:38.264 --> 01:39.557
MEMORIES OF MIDDLE SCHOOL

01:39.641 --> 01:40.642
A little.

01:40.725 --> 01:42.393
So she's shy around strangers...

01:48.358 --> 01:49.692
Hikawa.

01:51.194 --> 01:54.280
Are you maybe scared of me too?

01:54.364 --> 01:55.365
Huh?

01:57.742 --> 01:58.952
No.

01:59.035 --> 02:00.161
Not anymore.

02:00.662 --> 02:02.038
I'm not scared of you.

02:08.837 --> 02:10.547
Thank goodness.

02:15.260 --> 02:18.680
Of course. Amamiya is human too.

02:18.763 --> 02:21.266
He hurts, and worries over things too.

02:21.891 --> 02:24.144
This is all so obvious, and yet...

02:25.270 --> 02:28.773
Just how have I been treating him
all this time?

02:31.776 --> 02:33.194
Amamiya.

02:33.778 --> 02:36.447
Man, what do I do?
I can't look her in the face.

02:39.784 --> 02:40.785
Huh?

02:43.997 --> 02:45.915
- A co-co-co--
- Co?

02:45.999 --> 02:48.084
There! Down there! Behind you!

02:48.168 --> 02:50.628
Look! There! There!

02:50.712 --> 02:52.255
Huh? What?

03:00.013 --> 03:01.764
HEH - HAH

03:03.850 --> 03:05.059
Oh, my gosh...

03:06.978 --> 03:08.521
I thought you'd gone mad!

03:08.605 --> 03:11.524
Well, because... Sorry about that.

03:12.901 --> 03:16.029
I don't want to be friends
by me prying open the door.

03:16.863 --> 03:18.781
I want to know you for you.

03:18.865 --> 03:20.283
I want to be genuine friends.

03:20.867 --> 03:22.118
I want you to smile.

03:22.911 --> 03:24.203
That's all.

03:26.122 --> 03:27.540
That's all it was.

03:28.416 --> 03:29.834
And yet...

05:01.551 --> 05:05.972
EPISODE 9
SELF-AWARENESS

05:06.806 --> 05:08.474
They sure are taking their time.

05:10.810 --> 05:12.645
Isn't this way too long
for a little break?

05:12.729 --> 05:14.272
Do they even want to study?

05:14.355 --> 05:15.648
Exams are coming up, you know.

05:15.732 --> 05:18.026
- You're one to talk.
- Says you!

05:18.109 --> 05:20.153
OPERATION "SURPRISE THEM
WHEN THEY COME BACK"

05:21.779 --> 05:23.156
So, Yota.

05:23.823 --> 05:25.074
Who do you like?

05:26.743 --> 05:28.244
Why do you ask?

05:28.328 --> 05:33.166
Well, you never talk about this stuff.
So I'm curious.

05:38.796 --> 05:39.797
Miki.

05:39.881 --> 05:40.882
Huh?

05:46.846 --> 05:48.931
- Koyun.
- Huh?

05:49.015 --> 05:51.684
Hayato, Daichi, Gin.

05:51.768 --> 05:54.604
Mom, Dad, Haruto, Sakura.

05:54.687 --> 05:56.272
Whoa, slow down there.

05:56.355 --> 05:57.940
At least include Minato, please.

06:02.111 --> 06:03.696
Hey, Yota.

06:03.780 --> 06:09.035
If you ever do get a crush on someone,
I'll be right there to have your back.

06:09.535 --> 06:12.330
Seeing as you've done so much for me.

06:17.835 --> 06:20.213
- I knew I could count on you.
- Yeah!

06:21.798 --> 06:23.299
Hey, they're back.

06:24.801 --> 06:26.511
Huh? Where is everyone?

06:26.594 --> 06:29.138
All their stuff is still here.
Maybe they went to the bathroom?

06:31.557 --> 06:33.726
Well, wherever it is,
they'll be back soon.

06:34.227 --> 06:35.228
I guess you're right.

06:38.356 --> 06:43.486
The way Yota suppresses his feelings
in order to stay friends with Miki...

06:44.153 --> 06:46.239
I can tell it's draining him.

06:47.073 --> 06:51.244
And similarly, if Hikawa falls for Yota,

06:51.744 --> 06:53.996
he won't return the feelings.

06:54.831 --> 06:56.499
She really shouldn't go there...

06:57.291 --> 06:59.001
Or so I thought.

07:00.002 --> 07:04.340
But really, these aren't the things that
you can just will in and out of existence.

07:07.718 --> 07:09.512
I wish I hadn't noticed this.

07:10.596 --> 07:13.808
It feels like she's finally
opened up a little to me.

07:14.600 --> 07:17.395
- So I can't just barge in and--
- Amamiya.

07:21.149 --> 07:22.275
Here.

07:22.358 --> 07:24.861
I've only got two left.
So take it while you can.

07:29.157 --> 07:30.408
Thank you.

07:33.035 --> 07:34.162
This sucks...

07:34.245 --> 07:35.246
POPPING OUT

07:35.329 --> 07:37.498
- "Take it while you can?" Ouch!
- You were here?

07:43.212 --> 07:44.213
ART ROOM

07:44.297 --> 07:46.757
Have you always had lunch here
in the Art Room, Tsukiko?

07:46.841 --> 07:51.137
Yeah. I can finish my lunch early here
and then get straight back to work.

07:52.889 --> 07:54.265
Very practical.

07:54.348 --> 07:56.350
APPEARED IN EP 6
GRADE 1 CLASS 2 - LIBRARY REP

07:56.434 --> 07:57.768
I'm Tsukiko Shimojima.

07:58.436 --> 08:02.523
I did start out eating
with everyone in the classroom.

08:02.607 --> 08:05.860
But we had a pretty big group, and
it's not like we were all best buddies.

08:05.943 --> 08:07.653
GROUP THAT JUST CAME TO BE
SAME MIDDLE SCHOOL - FRIENDS

08:07.737 --> 08:09.030
SAME CLUB - SIT TOGETHER
ALWAYS CHATTING

08:09.113 --> 08:15.786
We also had this unspoken rule that we all
had to wait for everyone before we'd eat.

08:15.870 --> 08:20.291
I thought to myself, "Wait,
is this really what close friends do?"

08:20.374 --> 08:24.295
So I started distancing myself,
and kind of broke away from the group.

08:24.378 --> 08:25.796
HAHA

08:27.632 --> 08:30.843
But it's not that I left
on bad terms or anything.

08:30.927 --> 08:33.012
I still hang out with everyone separately.

08:33.513 --> 08:37.141
Oh, no! Now she's going
to think I'm a terrible person.

08:37.225 --> 08:38.559
I get it.

08:39.143 --> 08:41.812
I get it so much that now I feel sick.

08:41.896 --> 08:43.481
Empathy.

08:43.564 --> 08:45.233
Are you okay?

08:45.733 --> 08:49.070
Well, I'm not very good
at operating in groups either.

08:49.570 --> 08:51.822
Honestly, I can see it.

08:51.906 --> 08:54.075
LOOKING

08:56.160 --> 08:57.328
Oh, man.

08:57.411 --> 09:00.831
If only we'd been able to chat sooner.

09:02.917 --> 09:04.043
YAY

09:04.126 --> 09:05.461
Strawberries today.

09:05.545 --> 09:06.921
Would you like some?

09:07.004 --> 09:08.339
Are you sure?

09:08.422 --> 09:11.342
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

09:11.425 --> 09:13.052
AFTER SCHOOL STUDY SESSION

09:13.135 --> 09:14.845
So, curry...

09:15.930 --> 09:17.098
Anyone want curry?

09:17.181 --> 09:18.599
- Huh?
- What?

09:18.683 --> 09:21.477
I mean, when do we ever not want curry?

09:21.561 --> 09:23.604
You're on board! I like you.

09:24.397 --> 09:28.109
So, there's apparently this famous curry
place at the new mall that just opened up.

09:28.192 --> 09:29.318
MAKE A LITTLE PIT STOP

09:29.402 --> 09:30.528
- Can we go?
- Sure.

09:30.611 --> 09:31.904
COVERED BY THEIR COMMUTER PASS

09:31.988 --> 09:34.282
But it'll mean you two will have
to ride the train with us.

09:34.365 --> 09:35.408
I don't mind.

09:35.491 --> 09:36.492
Me neither.

09:36.576 --> 09:38.411
What about dinner at home?

09:38.494 --> 09:42.039
Koyun. You're always
worrying about that. I'll be fine.

09:42.123 --> 09:43.124
"Always"?

09:43.207 --> 09:47.128
All right! Then we're having an outing!

09:47.211 --> 09:49.630
STATION - SCHOOL
TROT TROT TROT

09:50.548 --> 09:51.632
Wow.

09:51.716 --> 09:54.927
- Is that where you hold on?
- Yes?

09:55.011 --> 09:56.053
- So jealous.
- Jealous?

09:56.137 --> 09:57.138
SPARKLE SPARKLE

09:57.722 --> 09:59.765
I don't need to hold onto anything.
I can stand.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.309
Core! Strength!

10:01.392 --> 10:02.977
So, that's how you're competing?

10:06.063 --> 10:07.106
You're heavy.

10:07.189 --> 10:08.649
That's not holding your own.

10:08.733 --> 10:10.651
I'm not using my hands,
so it still counts.

10:10.735 --> 10:12.153
No way does that count.

10:25.791 --> 10:29.795
Things have changed so much
from how they were not too long ago.

10:33.049 --> 10:38.888
Middle school felt like a fish tank,
and me a creature that couldn't breathe.

10:39.889 --> 10:42.808
I couldn't be like the others,
and that pained me.

10:43.809 --> 10:46.145
I realized I was living
somewhere where I didn't belong.

10:47.188 --> 10:50.149
But even when I fled,
there was no place to belong.

10:50.733 --> 10:53.527
I felt like I was at fault
for not being able to adapt.

10:54.320 --> 10:56.739
It hurt... It hurt so much...

10:57.823 --> 10:58.824
But then...

11:00.493 --> 11:02.912
Then I found my way out of the fish tank

11:03.829 --> 11:07.333
and I realized I didn't have to endure
the pain of living in a small world.

11:07.416 --> 11:10.586
Once I realized I didn't have to settle,

11:12.004 --> 11:14.423
it all seemed so trivial.

11:17.510 --> 11:18.511
STUDENT COUNCIL NEWSLETTER

11:18.594 --> 11:20.012
DEAR STUDENTS, CONGRATULATIONS
ON ENTERING HIGH SCHOOL

11:20.096 --> 11:21.931
Club activities,
school events, even friends...

11:22.014 --> 11:24.433
If I could just spend
the next three years in peace,

11:25.059 --> 11:26.852
then none of that even matters.

11:31.315 --> 11:33.526
Things have changed a lot since then.

11:34.527 --> 11:38.072
Wow, it's so nice here
around the train station now.

11:39.073 --> 11:41.492
Or maybe I've changed as well?

11:42.410 --> 11:45.121
It's so different
compared to before the mall was here.

11:45.204 --> 11:47.331
I'll bet the rent around here
has gone bonkers.

11:47.415 --> 11:48.624
Who are you to judge?

11:49.125 --> 11:51.168
Yeah. Everything will be fine.

11:52.169 --> 11:56.006
I can just pretend
those bad memories don't exist.

11:56.674 --> 12:00.594
GRAND OPENING SALE

12:01.720 --> 12:06.016
Let's see. We're here,
and the food court is here, so...

12:06.100 --> 12:07.101
FOOD COURT

12:07.184 --> 12:08.185
This way.

12:08.269 --> 12:09.478
POWER WALKING - GAH

12:09.562 --> 12:12.523
I knew you'd come to that conclusion.
It's the opposite direction.

12:12.606 --> 12:13.607
JEEZ

12:13.691 --> 12:15.401
Here. It's this way.

12:15.484 --> 12:17.570
Are you sure?
You're not tricking me, are you?

12:17.653 --> 12:19.113
I'm sure.

12:19.196 --> 12:21.699
Hey, what was that "I know you"
attitude just now?

12:21.782 --> 12:22.783
I can get behind this!

12:22.867 --> 12:23.868
FLASH
POWERED BY FAN LOVE

12:30.124 --> 12:31.208
Really?

12:34.462 --> 12:35.754
Whoa...

12:36.464 --> 12:38.799
- Miki.
- Whoa! Personal space, dude! What is it?

12:38.883 --> 12:41.260
- Igarashi's here.
- What?

12:42.303 --> 12:44.346
We don't get along anymore.

12:44.930 --> 12:47.349
We should keep him away from Hikawa, yeah?

12:49.685 --> 12:51.270
So, Koyun told you?

12:51.770 --> 12:53.355
That they used to date.

12:53.439 --> 12:55.774
Yeah. Very briefly though.

12:56.275 --> 12:57.860
That they're on bad terms.

12:58.444 --> 13:01.322
Do you think it'll turn into a fight
if they do run into each other?

13:01.405 --> 13:04.158
No, I don't think it'd go that far.

13:04.241 --> 13:07.369
Well, either way,
I don't want Hikawa feeling bad.

13:07.453 --> 13:08.621
Let's keep them apart.

13:09.205 --> 13:10.414
Agreed.

13:16.545 --> 13:17.838
What's up, Koyun?

13:18.672 --> 13:19.757
Can't let him see.

13:20.257 --> 13:21.884
- Yota, look! A dog.
- What?

13:21.967 --> 13:23.302
Let's go see it.

13:23.385 --> 13:26.096
But then, maybe nothing will happen.

13:26.180 --> 13:29.391
He could have actually moved on already.

13:29.475 --> 13:31.894
Yeah, I guess you're right.

13:32.520 --> 13:34.146
Hikawa?

13:34.230 --> 13:37.024
I don't remember anyone
by that name from middle school.

13:39.610 --> 13:43.155
Still, to have supposedly forgotten
she even existed...

13:43.739 --> 13:48.202
Well, I guess all we can do is hope
that he gets on with his next girlfriend.

13:48.786 --> 13:50.162
What?

13:50.246 --> 13:52.998
Oh, sorry. Just saying random things.

13:53.082 --> 13:56.669
I don't know anything about Igarashi's
love life since we started high school.

13:56.752 --> 13:58.546
Maybe he's still single?

13:58.629 --> 14:01.131
- Maybe he's taken? Who knows.
- Girlfriend?

14:02.758 --> 14:03.759
What?

14:05.719 --> 14:07.638
- What a lovely meal.
- What a lovely meal.

14:07.721 --> 14:10.182
Yeah! Outta my way!

14:10.266 --> 14:11.267
Would you pipe down?

14:13.852 --> 14:17.940
- I'll be damned if anyone beats me!
- Oh, man. Someone's using it.

14:18.023 --> 14:19.525
- Get back here!
- Let's go elsewhere.

14:19.608 --> 14:20.734
MATSURI - ONDO NO MASTER

14:20.818 --> 14:21.986
There! There! There!

14:22.069 --> 14:23.070
Ouch!

14:23.153 --> 14:24.530
Sorry, Yota!

14:24.613 --> 14:25.614
UPPI PURI

14:25.698 --> 14:26.824
A photo while we're here!

14:26.907 --> 14:28.409
Am I even allowed in this thing?

14:28.492 --> 14:29.618
Why wouldn't you be?

14:29.702 --> 14:31.120
I get nervous.

14:31.620 --> 14:34.790
Ready? Three, two, one...

14:34.874 --> 14:35.875
Yay!

14:37.293 --> 14:40.546
Welp, that was so much fun.

14:40.629 --> 14:43.299
I love this guilty pleasure
of messing around before exams.

14:43.382 --> 14:44.758
I could get hooked.

14:44.842 --> 14:46.886
Please don't get addicted.

14:46.969 --> 14:48.804
We'll hit the books again tomorrow.

14:49.930 --> 14:51.807
Yota!

14:52.683 --> 14:53.809
See you!

14:54.393 --> 14:55.644
- See you.
- Bye-bye.

15:00.941 --> 15:02.943
WE ARE
ADORBS

15:03.736 --> 15:05.613
- Good for you.
- What? Don't know what you mean.

15:05.696 --> 15:06.697
GRINNING - PRICKLY

15:09.992 --> 15:13.704
I guess all we can do is hope
that he gets on with his next girlfriend.

15:14.288 --> 15:17.291
Come on, man. Of course she's going
to have had past relationships.

15:17.958 --> 15:21.795
But honestly? With Igarashi?
It's just too out there.

15:22.796 --> 15:29.219
I kind of get how she'd have...
feelings for Yota, but...

15:29.929 --> 15:31.889
No. I don't want to "get" that.

15:34.433 --> 15:35.434
BONK

15:35.517 --> 15:37.478
- Oh, man.
- Hey, what's up?

15:37.561 --> 15:40.230
I don't get it at all.

15:44.485 --> 15:46.487
Told you. 'Vators are the best.

15:46.570 --> 15:50.950
You Azumis are the only ones I know
who call elevators "'vators"...

15:59.708 --> 16:01.168
Back in middle school,

16:02.252 --> 16:04.505
I hated Tsubasa Igarashi.

16:05.089 --> 16:06.757
- Looks lame.
- Our misaligned personalities.

16:06.840 --> 16:09.009
- It's serious, man.
- His unrequited love for me.

16:10.344 --> 16:13.013
- Come, now. She's got Igarashi.
- Everyone ignoring my feelings.

16:13.097 --> 16:15.641
- Don't keep Igarashi waiting.
- Everyone only wanting a good time.

16:15.724 --> 16:18.268
I hated everything. Everything.

16:19.770 --> 16:23.440
But that's not the reason
I want to avoid talking about him.

16:24.817 --> 16:27.778
It's because of what I did to him.

16:30.406 --> 16:31.407
You.

16:34.618 --> 16:36.161
What's with the hair?

16:36.245 --> 16:37.246
WHOA

16:37.329 --> 16:38.831
M-Me?

16:38.914 --> 16:41.417
It was some wild color
the last time I saw you too.

16:41.500 --> 16:43.252
MATCH HIS VIBES FOR NOW
FIDGET FIDGET

16:43.335 --> 16:45.754
So, what?
I look good no matter what, am I right?

16:45.838 --> 16:47.172
Gosh, your fidgeting is gross.

16:47.798 --> 16:50.676
He's acting like I'm not even here.

16:52.469 --> 16:54.471
I'm out of that fish tank,

16:55.514 --> 16:59.268
but the more I get to know myself,
the more I hate myself.

17:02.604 --> 17:03.647
I...

17:04.148 --> 17:08.068
I never liked you. Not even for a second.

17:08.652 --> 17:13.574
I've been too afraid
to face the one I hurt with my own malice.

17:14.491 --> 17:15.909
I'm nothing but a coward.

17:18.162 --> 17:19.163
See you.

17:24.418 --> 17:25.419
Igarashi.

17:31.091 --> 17:32.092
What do you want?

17:33.969 --> 17:36.096
Are you enjoying high school?

17:38.098 --> 17:41.602
What? Are you
some long-lost relative, or something?

17:41.685 --> 17:42.728
GONG

17:42.811 --> 17:44.229
Crap... What to do?

17:44.313 --> 17:46.356
That clapback was actually hilarious.

17:47.066 --> 17:49.401
I knew it. We can't converse.

17:49.902 --> 17:51.028
I'm fine.

17:52.154 --> 17:54.948
And it's not like I need
your concern, either.

18:00.829 --> 18:04.416
You really surprised me there
when you stopped Igarashi like that.

18:04.500 --> 18:06.502
EPISODE: TALKING A BIT MORE
BEFORE WE GO HOME

18:06.585 --> 18:07.586
Thanks.

18:08.754 --> 18:09.922
I wonder why I did it?

18:10.005 --> 18:13.759
I had so much fun with you guys today,
eating dinner and stuff.

18:13.842 --> 18:15.052
Maybe that's why?

18:15.552 --> 18:17.096
I definitely acted out of character.

18:17.679 --> 18:18.764
Koyun.

18:26.355 --> 18:28.357
Here. Thanks for this.

18:28.440 --> 18:30.984
Excuse me? What's with the bag?

18:31.068 --> 18:35.864
Who cares? It's not like you're gonna see
anyone on your way home.

18:37.533 --> 18:40.119
I did. And it was her, of all people...

18:40.702 --> 18:42.871
Are you enjoying high school?

18:43.497 --> 18:45.040
You're one to talk.

18:47.626 --> 18:48.627
What a pain.

18:52.881 --> 18:53.882
Say...

18:54.466 --> 18:57.803
You only went out with Igarashi
because of me, right?

18:58.428 --> 19:02.850
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have spoken out
of turn without considering your feelings.

19:04.810 --> 19:05.811
What?

19:05.894 --> 19:07.312
What?

19:07.396 --> 19:09.898
You spoke out of turn?

19:09.982 --> 19:12.359
Yeah, didn't I?

19:12.442 --> 19:14.069
We were here once before, chatting,

19:14.153 --> 19:16.822
where I told you it's "good enough"
and you're being "greedy."

19:16.905 --> 19:19.741
You did? Maybe...

19:19.825 --> 19:22.035
What? That's it?

19:22.119 --> 19:24.204
Sorry, my memory's a bit hazy.

19:24.288 --> 19:25.289
CONFUSED

19:25.372 --> 19:28.292
What? Then why did you two date?

19:31.545 --> 19:32.880
- It's a secret.
- What?

19:32.963 --> 19:33.964
SHOCK

19:34.590 --> 19:38.552
If I tell you,
you're gonna look down on me.

19:38.635 --> 19:39.720
Hey, hold up...

19:41.471 --> 19:43.640
That comment is not allowed to slide.

19:43.724 --> 19:44.725
Such force...

19:46.768 --> 19:47.811
I...

19:48.937 --> 19:52.691
I thought I'd feel better
if I fell in love with somebody

19:52.774 --> 19:54.234
who actually loves me.

19:55.485 --> 19:58.488
But I didn't feel better.
In fact, it only made things worse.

19:59.531 --> 20:01.658
And in the end,
I only wound up hurting Igarashi.

20:02.868 --> 20:05.204
Or rather,
I went out of my way to hurt him.

20:06.538 --> 20:08.707
I was acting in a way
that went against my heart.

20:08.790 --> 20:10.959
All I could think about was myself.

20:11.835 --> 20:15.255
And, Miki... You hate people who do that.

20:17.507 --> 20:19.009
I have nothing to say to that.

20:19.593 --> 20:24.598
I mean, no matter what you did,
Igarashi was going to get hurt, right?

20:24.681 --> 20:27.267
And that's not your fault, or anything.

20:27.851 --> 20:32.898
And besides. I wouldn't know
how to hate you even if I tried.

20:32.981 --> 20:35.234
And I'd never hate you
over something like that.

20:35.317 --> 20:36.318
BASHFUL

20:36.401 --> 20:37.402
OH?

20:37.486 --> 20:38.987
All right!

20:39.071 --> 20:42.115
Let's overwrite these sucky memories
with new, happy relationships.

20:42.199 --> 20:44.368
No, thank you.

20:44.451 --> 20:46.119
You can do that for the both of us.

20:46.203 --> 20:48.789
- Who would be good for you?
- What?

20:48.872 --> 20:49.915
(IGNORING)
WHAT SORT OF PERSON...

20:50.499 --> 20:53.168
I'd like someone who's
the complete opposite to Igarashi for you.

20:53.252 --> 20:55.420
Someone kind, with his head in the clouds.

20:55.504 --> 20:58.423
Someone who can meet you at your pace.

20:59.007 --> 21:03.053
I'd like someone who likes you for you.

21:03.136 --> 21:06.181
Someone kind, and with a big heart.

21:07.391 --> 21:09.643
- No, don't bother about me.
- No, don't bother about me.

21:09.726 --> 21:11.687
JINX

21:14.773 --> 21:17.901
Well, it's not like dating is
the be-all and end-all.

21:17.985 --> 21:20.028
I'm having plenty of fun
just as we are now.

21:20.112 --> 21:23.657
But a little love could be
just the cherry on top, right?

21:23.740 --> 21:25.784
Like a cherry tomato in your bento.

21:27.411 --> 21:29.204
Is that the right saying?

21:29.288 --> 21:30.664
Who even knows.

21:31.540 --> 21:32.749
Love.

21:32.833 --> 21:36.670
Koyuki, do you like Igarashi?

21:38.338 --> 21:39.589
No, I don't.

21:40.090 --> 21:41.883
That's just what people are saying.

21:42.592 --> 21:43.677
I see...

21:46.013 --> 21:47.264
You know what?

21:47.347 --> 21:50.350
Atagawa's been really
coming on strong with me lately.

21:51.518 --> 21:54.730
I'm not interested in anyone
other than the person I like.

21:54.813 --> 21:56.815
Honestly, it's getting annoying.

22:04.573 --> 22:05.824
Hey, Miki.

22:06.533 --> 22:09.619
My heart isn't as pure as yours.

22:09.703 --> 22:11.788
- See you.
- I'll await your tomato report.

22:11.872 --> 22:13.582
Personally...

22:13.665 --> 22:14.875
Tomato report! I love it.

22:14.958 --> 22:16.668
I could never recommend myself to anyone.

22:18.337 --> 22:19.504
So...

22:22.841 --> 22:24.843
You find happiness, Miki.

23:50.345 --> 23:55.350
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
